<DocsExample TExample="ResponsiveCurrentWidthExample" Title="What renders at this width" Description="Each row is wrapped in an NTResponsive that is visible at or above its Material 3 breakpoint (Direction defaults to Above). Resize the window and rows appear or disappear. The wrapper uses display: contents, so it adds no layout box." />
<DocsExample TExample="ResponsiveSwapExample" Title="Swapping content" Description="Pair an Above and a Below rule on the same breakpoint to show one layout on wide screens and another on narrow ones." />
<DocsExample TExample="ResponsiveHideExample" Title="Hiding content" Description="Visibility=Hide removes the content on the targeted side of the breakpoint. Here the shortcut hint is hidden on narrow windows." />
<DocsExample TExample="ResponsiveCustomBreakpointExample" Title="Custom breakpoint" Description="CustomBreakpoint overrides Breakpoint with an exact pixel width." />
